body:
This doesn't look correct as it will always copy the data.

The mirror pattern works like this:
```
LocalVector buffer[2];
LocalVector * curr = buffer[0];
LocalVector * prev = buffer[1];

// Swap
SWAP(curr, prev);
```
You are thus only swapping a pointer, and not the data.
You can do the same with indices too.

When you access, you access via the pointers.

